Z||000001||TheFiero64||01-09-2001||03:14 PM||||formula 2001 is the best I've used<BR><P>------------------<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||3
Z||000002||jerpro||01-09-2001||03:40 PM||||I side with the fiero 64||||reg||1
Z||000003||2xsess||01-09-2001||06:23 PM||||I used to use that too (formula 2001)<P>But I bought a bottle of Armor All high gloss and that is some awesome stuff. Although it doesn't seem to stay shiny as long as the 2001.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroJoe||01-09-2001||06:57 PM||||I use armor all, and a lot of it.  I've used Finish 2001 before, and have had good results with it too.  I use armor all on radiator hoses, my intake hose, plug wires, anything that needs to be protected.<BR>I've been thinking of trying a few other brands, but for now I'll just use my armor all, mostly because I found a gallon of it in my grandpa's basement and he let me have it.<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||01-09-2001||08:12 PM||||I know everyone 'loves' ArmourAll. But...<BR>it covers all your rubber and vinyl with that nice shiny coating that look pretty and will prevent a lot of UV rays from attacking, but it also 'pulls' the plasicene, the part that keep stuff pliable, from within, only to let it eventually dry off. Sooner or later, itll get so brittle it will crack. I had a seat that literaly broke all over like an eggshell from years of armourall when I sat on it one day. Use a real rubber dressing on rubber parts, like hoses and tires, use something like "The Tannery" on our leather and vinyl. Or even saddle soap, which is made to keep leather soft forever. Dash and door panels can even use neutral paste shoe polish with great results. Armour All was sued a number of years ago in a group lawsuit for damage to cars that was caused by the product.<P>use what u want though, just my nickles worth. I do use it on cars I sell though, cheap way to make em look good, since Im not keeping them.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Cooter||01-09-2001||09:30 PM||||ArmorAll is petroleum (sp) based. Formula 2001 is water based. 2001 lasts a long time as long as it stays dry, it is not very long lasting on exterior stuff, but is great for interiors.||||reg||1
Z||000007||WampusCat||01-09-2001||10:20 PM||||303 protectant.  Works great on any kind of plastic/vinyl.  Not greasy feeling like armor all.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Hank is Here||01-09-2001||11:03 PM||||I like Maguires (sp).  Actually right now is a good time to keep your eyes open at Wal-Mart for car cleaning kits on sale.  I usually notice they pack like wash, wax, tire stuff, and dressing in gift packs for the holidays and about now they get really marked down.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Raydar||01-09-2001||11:41 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>I know everyone 'loves' ArmourAll. But...<BR>...I had a seat that literaly broke all over like an eggshell from years of armourall when I sat on it one day. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Same thing happened to me. Only car that I ever owned that was "ArmourAll'd" (by previous owner). Only car that ever had a vinyl seat cover to actually shatter. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Standard||01-10-2001||02:35 AM||||Usually French or Thousand Island...<P>oh wait a second  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I've never used ArmourAll, but I hate that greasy film it puts on...||||reg||12
Z||000011||stsmithgt||01-10-2001||06:59 PM||||2001 has done a good job for me.  It doesn't smell too strong, it lasts, it has that UV protectant in it, and if you call in the next 10 minutes, you can get a handy little pocket size for FREE!!! <P>j\k  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><BR>I do have a small bottle in my center glove box for when I wipe the dust off my dash. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by stsmithgt (edited 01-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||Seanh||01-10-2001||11:30 PM||||Well, I hate Armor All. I would never use it, makes the surface way to shiny and it reflects in the windows. I, by far, would use Lexol brand vinyl cleaner/conditioner. The only place Iv found it is Pep-Boys, but I live in a small town and not to many automotive places here. I really like it, cleans it great, gets all the black crap off it, and doesnt make it shine to bad.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>"It's always in the last place you look." Of course it is. Why would you keep looking after you've found it? Do people do this? Who and where are they?</I>||||reg||1
Z||000013||GT Bastard||01-11-2001||02:32 PM||||I would have to agree with Meguires Vinyl and rubber cleaner...  It cleans and conditions the surface, and it smells nice.  Spendier than most other though.  It's worth the extra money.  The detail shop I work for recently switched to Automagic dressings, which don't seem to do quite as well.  ||||reg||1
Z||000014||stsmithgt||01-11-2001||04:31 PM||||Oh yeah, Meguire's.  They make a lot of nice products.  I forgot about them.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">||||reg||1
